.TH DASHBOARD 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dashboard \- single-page solar energy-flow dashboard with a Prometheus proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dashboard
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serves the pv-suite dashboard (a single static page: the animated
energy-flow diagram, the energy summary, the zoomable time-series chart,
the CSV exports, dark/light themes, EN/PL i18n) and proxies
\fB/prom/*\fR to a Prometheus upstream with the query string preserved \(em
same-origin for the browser, no CORS and no mixed content. The page is
read-only; when Prometheus is unreachable it falls back to a DEMO DATA
mode so the layout still renders.
.PP
The page expects the \fBhuawei_*\fR metrics from
.BR modbus-scraper (1)
(Prometheus job name \fBsun2000\fR). User settings live in
\fBconfig.js\fR next to the server (served at \fB/config.js\fR): the
Prometheus URL, the metric selectors, the scrape/smoothing/refresh
windows, the battery switch. URL parameters override everything for
testing (\fB?prom=...&pv=...&battery=1&lang=...\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
the server ini (same keys, snake_case, \fB[server]\fR section). Default
\fBserver.ini\fR next to the script.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
listen port. Default \fB8080\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " HOST"
bind address. Default \fB0.0.0.0\fR \-\- pass \fB127.0.0.1\fR for
loopback-only.
.TP
.BI \-\-upstream " URL"
the Prometheus base URL. Default \fBhttp://localhost:9090\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-prom-prefix " PATH"
the path prefix proxied to Prometheus. Default \fB/prom\fR; empty proxies
every unmatched path.
.TP
.BI \-\-static-dir " DIR"
the directory to serve. Default \fBstatic\fR next to the script.
.TP
.BI \-\-config-js " FILE"
the user settings file to serve at \fB/config.js\fR. Default
\fBconfig.js\fR next to the script; a missing file makes
\fB/config.js\fR 404 and the page boots with built-in defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-battery
inject \fBbattery: true\fR into the served \fBconfig.js\fR (the Battery
node, the three-way energy split).
.TP
.BI \-\-log-level " LEVEL" ", " \-\-log-queries
default \fBINFO\fR; proxied queries log at DEBUG, or at INFO with
\fB--log-queries\fR.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
shutdown.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PORT ", " BIND ", " PROM_URL ", " PROM_PREFIX
the flag twins (the flags win).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I dashboard/src/server.ini
the packaged sample config.
.TP
.I dashboard/src/config.js
the user settings (served at \fB/config.js\fR).
.TP
.I dashboard/src/static/vendor/echarts.min.js
the vendored Apache ECharts 5.5.1 (Apache-2.0) \(em the suite's only
third-party code.
.SH SECURITY
The page and the proxy carry no authentication. Widen the bind
deliberately and put an authenticating reverse proxy in front for LAN or
internet exposure (nginx/Caddy examples in \fBdashboard/README.md\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-scraper (1),
.BR modbus-cache (1)
.PP
\fBdashboard/README.md\fR in the suite checkout \(em the config keys, the
URL parameters and the reverse-proxy recipes.
